    <span class="badge">Chapter 1 Analysis</span>
    <h1>Recognition of Need</h1>
    <p>A formal system investigation of bKash Limited—evaluating organizational frameworks, operational models, and critical performance limitations[cite: 1].</p>

    <hr class="section-divider">

    <h2>1.1 Introduction & Background</h2>
    <p>bKash was founded in 2010 as a joint venture between Money in Motion LLC and BRAC Bank, officially launching on 21 July 2011 to bridge Bangladesh's unbanked population with expanding mobile communications[cite: 1]. Today, it operates with over 1,700 employees, nearly 300,000 agents, and 300,000 nationwide merchants[cite: 1].</p>

    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin: 16px 0 24px 0;">
      <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); border: 1px solid var(--border-card); padding: 18px; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>Business-to-Consumer (B2C) Model</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">Direct individual services including Cash-In, Cash-Out, P2P Send Money, Mobile Recharge, and Utility Payments executed via USSD (*247#) and the smartphone application[cite: 1].</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); border: 1px solid var(--border-card); padding: 18px; border-radius: 10px;">
        <h3>Business-to-Business (B2B) Model</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0;">Enterprise and corporate disbursement tools facilitating cashless corporate payrolls, merchant checkout collections, vendor settlements, and gateway API integrations[cite: 1].</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="section-divider">

    <h2>1.2 Problem Identification</h2>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><strong>Problem 01: Lack of International Payment Collaboration:</strong> The platform lacks direct interoperability with major global transaction services like PayPal, restricting freelancers, remote earners, and digital exporters from receiving international payments[cite: 1].</li>
      <li><strong>Problem 02: Server Traffic Management & Unconfirmed Transactions:</strong> Peak transaction periods cause synchronization bottlenecks where user balances are debited without prompt confirmation notifications, increasing anxiety and helpline traffic[cite: 1].</li>
      <li><strong>Problem 03: High Cash-Out and Send Money Charges:</strong> Uniform percentage-based tariffs create a heavy financial barrier for lower-income users who execute frequent micro-transfers, pushing them toward informal cash routes[cite: 1].</li>
      <li><strong>Problem 04: Low Daily Transaction Limits:</strong> Uniform daily regulatory ceilings do not adequately accommodate high-value transfers needed by small business operators and emergencies, forcing multi-day transaction splits[cite: 1].</li>
    </ul>

